  "_dpsWeightNote": "Retribution 4.31 and levelling 4.31 are derived from mechanics: 1 Strength = 2 AP = 0.232 dps for a paladin, so 1 weapon dps = 1/0.232 = 4.31 Strength. Holy 0.086 follows the same ratio off its near-zero Strength weight. Protection is the exception: the same derivation gave 2.37, which put pure-DPS Naxxramas one-hand swords (The Hungering Cold, Gressil, Andonisus) at the top of the tank weapon list. A tank's threat comes overwhelmingly from Holy damage -- Seal and Judgement of Righteousness, Consecration, Holy Shield -- which scales off spell power and attack power, not weapon dps, so the ratio does not transfer. Swept 0.0 to 2.37 against Wowhead's Classic Naxxramas tank BiS guide; 0.0 and 0.5 tie for best agreement and 0.5 is chosen as the physically non-zero end of that tie.",
  "_weightProvenance": "Ordinal priorities taken from Icy Veins TBC Classic stat-priority pages for each spec, then adapted for LEVELLING rather than raiding. That adaptation matters: the published priorities are for level-70 raiding, where hit-to-9%-cap, expertise and armour penetration dominate. Levelling gear from 1-69 carries almost none of those stats and the caps are irrelevant, so raw Strength, weapon damage and survivability stay ahead of them here. These are ordinal-derived, NOT sim-derived, and are the part of this model most worth Henrik's judgement -- editable live in the review page."
 },
